        "date": "2026-11-11T04:53:15Z"
      },
      "message": "refactor(sim): a field column's floor under a cut reads exactly by the monotone law\n\n#637 step E1. Every tool Stock::simulate builds spans the verdict world\nabove its tip, so its swept solid holds every point above any point it\nholds: a column's material is one interval [shell floor, tool bottom] or\nnothing, and a cut from above never raises the floor. SdfField::column_span\nreads both sides: the down-march's Top proves the shell floor; NoMaterial\nis cut through or a sub-cell sliver, told apart by the cut layer's own\nray-entry record at the cell below the floor plane. A tool that does not\nspan (a truncated taper, a bare ball, a lathe sweep, a posed axis) sets\nbounded_cuts and keeps step B's CutFromBelow refusal. floor_at keeps its\nAPI; CarriedField::column_body now carries through-holes and slivers\ninstead of refusing the carry.\n\nThe step E design (the holders' mutation path, baking the turn's signed\npermutation into the bricks, the upward march) is on the issue and in\ndocs/decisions/637-carried-stock-field.md; E2a-c are #779, #780, #781.\n\nNothing shipped changes: the column engine stays the default and the\nfield's down-march is untouched.\n\nRefs #637\nRefs #26\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
